# Ticket: Microsoft Teams Not Loading

**Scenario:**  
User reports that Microsoft Teams will not open on their workstation.  
They receive a message stating they do not have permission or that the 
app is unavailable.

**First Response to User:**  
Thanks for reaching out — I can help you with this.  
Let’s check a few things to narrow down the issue:

-- Are you receiving a specific error message when opening Teams?
-- Have you recently changed your password or signed in on a new device?
-- Are you able to access other Microsoft 365 apps (Outlook, OneDrive, SharePoint)?
-- Are you signed into Teams with your usual work account?

**Internal Notes:**  
-- User reports Teams shows “You don’t have access to this” when launching  
-- Confirmed user is signed in with correct work account  
-- User can access Outlook and SharePoint normally  
-- Checked Microsoft 365 Admin Center → user **does not** have a Teams-enabled license  
-- User assigned only an Exchange Online license  
-- Assigned Microsoft 365 Business Basic license to user  
-- Verified license assignment propagated  
-- Instructed user to sign out of Teams and sign back in  
-- User restarted Teams → app loads successfully and user can access chats 
and channels

**Resolution:**  
User was missing a Teams-enabled license.  
Assigned Microsoft 365 Business Basic license; Teams access restored.

**Root Cause:**  
Incorrect license assignment during onboarding.

**Preventive Notes:**  
Recommend verifying license bundles during account provisioning to ensure 
all required apps are included.
